 "notModeled": [
  "DATA INTERFACE CLOCK: the source-synchronous data clock DCLKOUT runs at 6x / 12x SMPL_CLK (24 bits x 8 channels / lanes / SDR-DDR per 4 SMPL_CLK periods, p.28 Equation 3); the schema's clockOut can only follow or divide the input clock, so DCLKOUT is not driven. Only FCLKOUT = SMPL_CLK / 4 is modeled",
  "data lanes: the model drives the 24-bit packets (18-bit result then six zeros) four bits per SMPL_CLK rising edge on D3..D0; the real lane assignment (4-lane: CH1-4 on D3/D2, CH5-8 on D1/D0; 2-lane: D3 and D1), SDR / DDR (DATA_RATE, DATA_LANES) and frame alignment to FCLKOUT (SMPL_SYNC) are not modeled; tOut uses the configuration SDO delay (16 ns), the data lanes are source-synchronous",
  "analog front end (PGA ranges RANGE_CHx, bandwidth ANA_BW, common-mode control, gain-error calibration, references): the result is always the 0 V code (0 two's complement, 20000h straight binary)",
  "output randomizer (XOR_EN), test patterns (TP_EN / TP_MODE fixed, ramp, alternating; TP0 / TP1), USER_BITS: stored only",
  "initialization sequence (Table 6-10: INIT_KEY, INIT, INIT_1..INIT_5 and the waits) is not required by the model; register fields are stored only",
  "SPI_EN low turns SDI into the EXTREF strap and disables the configuration port; the model always treats the port as enabled",
  "daisy-chain configuration (SPI_MODE = 0, DAISY_CHAIN_LEN, p.34-36): the model decodes every frame as a single device; SDO is driven 0 outside reads (the device drives 0 with SPI_MODE = 0 and Hi-Z with SPI_MODE = 1)",
  "register read in legacy mode needs SPI_RD_EN = 1 and SPI_MODE = 1; in that mode each 24-bit frame reads the addressed register in the selected bank (bank-0 addresses always), except address 00h which is still written (Figure 6-11 frame 4). Reads are listed per documented address; an undocumented address returns nothing",
  "register 00h is write-only; 06h (REG_00H_READBACK) is loaded with the value written to 00h by the write command (reset value 2h as documented)",
  "reserved bits are stored as written (\"do not change from the default\"); 04h bits 15-4 are read-only per the figure",
  "power-down: PWDN low or PD_CH = 11b / PD_CHIP; RESET pin low (registers to default); tPU 25 ms power-up, 5 us after reset",
  "SMPL_CLKM (differential sampling clock negative input) is ignored; single-ended SMPL_CLKP is the clock"
